#
# Pre-grant F-Droid the "install unknown apps" AppOp.
#
# Why this and not a permission grant: INSTALL_PACKAGES is signature|privileged and
# needs a priv-app plus an allowlist -- unreachable for us, because stripping the JNI
# libs forces a re-sign and the F-Droid Privileged Extension hardcodes F-Droid's own
# release certificate hash in ClientWhitelist. REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES is
# signature|appop with the AppOp defaulting to MODE_ERRORED, and it CANNOT be
# pre-granted declaratively -- DefaultPermissionGrantPolicy filters on
# perm.isRuntime(), which this is not. Setting the AppOp at runtime is the only route.
#
# Effect: the user never sees "Allow F-Droid to install unknown apps". They still
# confirm each individual install (that needs INSTALL_PACKAGES). Verified on k3-jun
# 2026-08-31: default state is "No operations / Default mode: default"; after this
# command, "REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES: allow".
#
# Runs every boot on purpose: AppOps state lives in /data/system/appops.xml, which
# survives reboots but not a /data reset.
#
# UNVERIFIED: whether init may exec /system/bin/cmd under SELinux without added
# policy. Test by pushing this to /product/etc/init/ over an adb-remount overlay and
# rebooting. If denied, the fallback is documenting the one-time Settings toggle.

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    exec -- /system/bin/cmd appops set org.fdroid.fdroid REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES allow
